NAME
    exit - leave Y1/OS for the ROM monitor

SYNOPSIS
    exit

DESCRIPTION
    Prints "bye" and returns to the ROM monitor's ">" prompt. Memory is
    left as it was, so a program loaded at $5000 can still be looked at
    with the monitor's B and D. The monitor's O boots Y1/OS again from
    the card: a fresh start in /. exit is a shell built-in, and the one
    word a /BIN program cannot replace (the shell checks it first).

EXAMPLES
    exit            then O at the monitor prompt to come back

NOTES
    Removed from the P8X version: the synonym mon (on Y1/OS, man mon
    describes the monitor itself).
    The command is the Y1/OS shell's own (os/y1os.c); the page is
    ported from P8X os/man/exit 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    mon
